  "prompt": "Recreate Video 1 shot for shot as realistic cinematic action footage with two new riders. The person from Image 1 takes the place of the man riding the invisible motorcycle, and the person from Image 2 takes the place of the man chasing him on the white motorcycle. Both perform exactly the same movements, poses, facial expressions and timing as in Video 1. Everything except the two riders stays exactly as in Video 1: the highway, background, camera, cuts, light and sound.\nRIDER 1 = Image 1: The man in front, who glides down the highway in a crouched riding pose without any visible vehicle, is exactly the person from Image 1, with the same face, hairstyle, hair color, age, height and overall appearance. He looks like the person in Image 1 in every shot, not like the man in Video 1 and not like a mix of both.\nRIDER 2 = Image 2: The man behind him, who chases him on the white futuristic motorcycle, is exactly the person from Image 2, with the same face, hairstyle, hair color, age, height and overall appearance. He looks like the person in Image 2 in every shot, not like the man in Video 1 and not like a mix of both.\nOUTFITS: Rider 1 wears exactly the outfit from Image 1 instead of the navy sweater, jeans and black shoes from Video 1. Rider 2 wears exactly the outfit from Image 2 instead of the dark blue jacket and light blue shirt from Video 1. Same garments, colors, patterns, prints, fabrics, fit, shoes and accessories as in the reference images, unchanged and consistent in every shot. No clothing from Video 1 is used. Never mix faces, hair or outfits between Image 1 and Image 2. Image 1 and Image 2 are used ONLY for the people and their outfits. Their backgrounds and settings are ignored and never appear in the video.\nTHE INVISIBLE MOTORCYCLE: Rider 1 has no vehicle at all. He crouches with bent knees and both arms stretched forward as if holding handlebars, and glides along the road on his shoes as if riding an invisible motorcycle. Do not add any motorcycle, board or object under him.\nTHE WHITE MOTORCYCLE: Rider 2's vehicle stays exactly as in Video 1: a glossy white futuristic motorcycle with round red lights on the handlebars and a glowing cyan ring headlight, casting a cyan glow on the road.\nSHOTS: Keep the same cuts at the same moments.\n0-5.2s: low tracking shot moving backward in front of rider 1 as he glides down a curved elevated highway ramp toward the camera in his crouched riding pose, leaning into the curve, concrete pillars, street lamps and a green road sign behind him. From around 3.5s, the cyan headlight of rider 2 appears far behind him.\n5.2-6.6s: cut to a close-up of rider 2 on the white motorcycle against a deep blue background, red handlebar lights and cyan ring headlight in front of him, staring forward with a serious, focused look.\n6.6-10s: cut to a low shot of rider 1 gliding toward the camera with rider 2 chasing close behind on the white motorcycle, round concrete towers in the background. At around 9s rider 1 does a full backflip in the air, then lands back in his crouched pose with both arms raised.\n10-12.2s: cut to a shot from behind rider 1 as he leans away, the white motorcycle rushes past the camera with motion blur, then a high wide view down the long curving highway ramp with both riders small in the distance and the cyan glow on the road.\n12.2-15s: cut to a low view down the ramp, rider 1 glides fast past the camera in his crouched pose, rider 2 follows close behind on the white motorcycle, then a side view of rider 2 speeding along the concrete barrier with motion blur.\nCAMERA: Same vertical 9:16 framing, same low, fast tracking camera moves, same angles, distances, motion blur and shot lengths as Video 1. Same number of shots and same shot order.\nSETTING: Same elevated concrete highway ramps at dusk, same grey asphalt with white and yellow lane lines, same concrete barriers, same huge round concrete pillars and towers, same street lamps and green road signs, same pale evening sky. Same soft, cool dusk light, plus the cyan glow of the motorcycle. Both riders and their outfits are lit by this same light so they fit naturally into the scene. Keep the same color grade and cinematic look as Video 1.\nSOUND: Same music and sound effects as Video 1, same timing.\nQUALITY: Real camera footage, natural realistic faces and hair, realistic fabric that moves with the wind and speed, natural hands with five fingers, stable identity and outfit in every shot. No distortion, no morphing, no extra vehicles, no CGI look, no beauty filter, no text."
